      "problem": "A newspaper in a town has $100\\,000$ subscribers, and $56\\,000$ of them have a digital subscription. If the newspaper randomly samples $224$ subscribers, find a normal approximation for the probability that between $112$ and $140$ subscribers (inclusive) in the sample have a digital subscription. You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.\n\n*Hint: Two tables of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.8\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0359\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0351\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0344\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0446\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0436\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0427\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0548\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0537\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0526\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.95